            <ArticleTitle>[Isolated exertion headache and Chiari's malformation].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>155-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 47 year-old woman had been suffering from exertional headache for 2 1/2 years. Neurological examination was normal. X-rays of the skull and cranio-cervical junction and CT were normal. MRI sagittal sections disclosed a Chiari type I malformation. The headache disappeared after occipital craniectomy and atlas laminectomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
